{Queen's Gambit Declined. Both sides have what they wanted from the opening. The middlegame will be about the centre.}
1. d4 d5 2. c4 c6 3. Nc3 e6 4. Nf3 Nf6 5. Bg5 Nbd7 {Theory ends about here. From this point the game is decided by understanding rather than memory.} 6. e3 Be7 7. Qc2 h6 8. Bh4 ! O-O {The point of the whole plan. Material is level, but only one side has a target to attack.} (8... dxc4 Rb1 c5 {was the alternative — playable, but it hands over the initiative.}) 9. Be2 dxc4 10. Bxc4 b5 11. Be2 Bb7 ?! 12. Rd1 Qb6 13. a3 Bd6 14. Bd3 Rfe8 15. O-O g6 16. Rfe1 Kg7 17. e4 e5 18. Bg3 exd4 19. Bxd6 dxc3 20. Qxc3 Rac8 21. b4 a6 22. Qb2 Qd8 23. e5 Nd5 24. e6+ Kg8 25. exd7 Qxd7 {Resignation is timely: the king cannot be defended and the counterplay is one move too slow.} 26. Bc5 1-0
